From f4c72a60bf54966d7a4d1f2a2b2190e0f2fc260a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Natanael Copa <ncopa@alpinelinux.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:44:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] s390/mm: fix build of do_secure_storage_access() backport

The backport of upstream commit b00be77302d7 ("s390/mm: Add missing
secure storage access fixups for donated memory") uses
&folio->flags.f, which depends on memdesc_flags_t introduced in v6.18
by commit 53fbef56e07d ("mm: introduce memdesc_flags_t"). In 6.12
folio->flags is still a plain unsigned long, so the build fails:

  arch/s390/mm/fault.c:448:59: error: request for member 'f' in something not a structure or union

Use &folio->flags like the other PG_arch_1 users in 6.12.

Fixes: 74ccc099f1ba ("s390/mm: Add missing secure storage access fixups for donated memory")
Signed-off-by: Natanael Copa <ncopa@alpinelinux.org>
---
 arch/s390/mm/fault.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/s390/mm/fault.c b/arch/s390/mm/fault.c
index 2d03af60ed88..4767f45629a9 100644
--- a/arch/s390/mm/fault.c
+++ b/arch/s390/mm/fault.c
@@ -445,7 +445,7 @@ void do_secure_storage_access(struct pt_regs *regs)
 			return;
 		rc = uv_convert_from_secure(folio_to_phys(folio));
 		if (!rc)
-			clear_bit(PG_arch_1, &folio->flags.f);
+			clear_bit(PG_arch_1, &folio->flags);
 		folio_put(folio);
 		/*
 		 * There are some valid fixup types for kernel
-- 
